{
  "schema": "dynsyslab.compute-job/v1",
  "kind": "experiment",
  "label": "rpe-coordinate-dynamics",
  "description": "Viscous RPE ring-down in three coordinate systems, (r,r') -> (e,e') -> xi_1..xi_4 (history of the echo alone), and SINDy rate laws within and across them. Train on IC 0 (r=2.3334), validate on held-out ICs r=1.25 and r=2.5 through the frozen training basis. Every coordinate change stores exact derivatives (system_derivatives) so fits learned from finite differences are scored against the analytic chain-rule reference, as in Codex's 5 November study.",
